From: gDiagram project
Subject: Fix vertical text centering in HTML table cells using font metrics

GraphViz HTML table cells (<TD>) render text above vertical center because
size_html_txt() uses raw font size as the baseline offset (lfsize[0] = mxfsize)
rather than the actual pango-measured baseline position within the logical
rectangle.

This patch computes lfsize[0] = maxlayout + maxoffset where:
  maxlayout = MAX(span->yoffset_layout) over all spans
            = distance from top of pango logical rectangle to baseline
  maxoffset = MAX(span->yoffset_centerline) over all spans
            = small above-baseline renderer correction (~0.05 * fontsize)

This places the rendered baseline at exactly the pango natural baseline
position, centering the logical rectangle in the cell. Also fixes the
non-pango fallback path in textspan.c to use fontsize as an estimate
for yoffset_layout (was 0.0, which collapsed the formula to lfsize ≈ 0).

Centering accuracy (14pt Times,serif, 36pt cell):
  Before patch:         3.71pt error (text too high)
  Old -2.0 hack:        1.71pt error
  This patch:           0.09pt error

The issue is visible when using HTML TABLE labels with cellpadding - text
appears shifted upward from the visual center of the cell.

--- a/lib/common/textspan.c
+++ b/lib/common/textspan.c
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ estimate_textspan_size(GVC_t * gvc, textspan_t * span)
     span->yoffset_centerline = 0.1 * span->font->size;
-    span->yoffset_layout = 0.0;
+    span->yoffset_layout = fontsize;  /* estimated: ascent ≈ 1× font size from top of logical rect */

--- a/lib/common/htmltable.c
+++ b/lib/common/htmltable.c
@@ -942,7 +942,7 @@ size_html_txt(graph_t * g, htxt_t * ftxt, htmlenv_t * env)
-    double maxoffset, mxysize = 0.0;
+    double maxoffset, maxlayout, mxysize = 0.0;

@@ -987,7 +987,7 @@ size_html_txt(graph_t * g, htxt_t * ftxt, htmlenv_t * env)
-    mxysize = maxoffset = mxfsize = 0;
+    mxysize = maxoffset = maxlayout = mxfsize = 0;

@@ -1031,6 +1031,7 @@ size_html_txt(graph_t * g, htxt_t * ftxt, htmlenv_t * env)
     maxoffset = MAX(lp.yoffset_centerline, maxoffset);
+    maxlayout = MAX(lp.yoffset_layout, maxlayout);

@@ -1047,7 +1047,11 @@ size_html_txt(graph_t * g, htxt_t * ftxt, htmlenv_t * env)
-    if (i == 0)
-        ftxt->spans[i].lfsize = mxfsize;
+    if (i == 0)
+        /* Place baseline using actual font metrics: centers the pango
+         * logical rectangle in the cell rather than approximating with
+         * raw font size. maxlayout = baseline distance from box top
+         * (yoffset_layout from the text layout engine); maxoffset =
+         * yoffset_centerline (small above-baseline correction applied
+         * by the renderer to convert from rendering origin to baseline). */
+        ftxt->spans[i].lfsize = maxlayout + maxoffset;
